", "adapter_description": "NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060", "vram_size": 7807}, "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "223284827", "author": {"steamid": "76561198007792140", "personaname": "Caim", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/CaimWasTaken/", "num_games_owned": 759, "num_reviews": 294, "playtime_forever": 10, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 10, "last_played": 1776222196, "avatar": "49185ccdecbfdee6f43fcefec89bb1b6c434ff79"}, "language": "english", "review": "You can tell when people that don't play games make them, that or there's a complete lack of good testers on their team.\n\nInsanely slow movement\n\nAnnoying camera effects you cannot disable\n\nSlowed down movement when swinging (mind you enemies everywhere shooting and swinging)\n\nSlowed down when channeling abilities (mind you enemies everywhere shooting and swinging)\n\n\"Clear the area\" objective but its a tower and a slime fell off somewhere and the arrows don't point to them until you're at the very top, and they were hidden propped up against a wall.\n\nNo direction, they took ror2 maps but made them aimless garbage.\n\nChests in home that comes off as a \"secret\" but its the same garbage outside that costs money, why even put them in there??????????\n\nToo much reading of weapon stats and what passives do in a TIMED game.\n\nGraphics, music, sfx, vfx, character design all forgettable. \n\nIt's like they took the combat design of the original Dungeon Defenders game but put it in a game that cannot use it.", "timestamp_created": 1776222502, "timestamp_updated": 1776222574, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 5, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.509828388690948486", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": true, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1769006794", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 31, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "223283730", 